Peak families already identify tetragonal scheelite CaWO₄ (e.g. 18.50, 28.57, 31.32, 34.03, 46.96°) and a second monoclinic WO₃ family (23.02/23.45/24.27°, 26.51°, 28.89°, 33.15°). I found a physically passing monoclinic WO₃ source whose transformed cell reproduces that family; an older competing WO₃ source triggers the supplied close-O review. I’m normalizing both passing alternatives plus plausible polymorph/residual candidates before the controlled whole-pattern comparison.

The controlled test is behaving as expected: scheelite alone leaves a large structured residual (Rwp ≈19.4% in the intentionally simple model). The scheelite + monoclinic WO₃ comparison is still refining; all atomic coordinates remain fixed and candidate scales are constrained nonnegative.

