The missing phase is now strongly supported: adding the physically passing Pnma Ca₃WO₆ analogue lowers the identical fixed-coordinate model from 13.48% to 9.35% Rwp and refines to ~12 wt%. This is a multi-line result, not a stick-only match. I’m completing monoclinic/tetragonal framework controls before choosing the parent and then will repeat all earlier deletion tests because the phase inventory changed.

All leading Ca₃WO₆ analogues remain physically passing after cell refinement. The monoclinic Sr₂MnWO₆-derived parent gives the best fixed-coordinate fit (9.23% Rwp), narrowly ahead of the Sr₂Fe and Pnma parents and far ahead of cubic/tetragonal controls. I’m selecting that parent provisionally and restarting nuisance tests from the three-phase inventory; prior WO₃ texture/size evidence is no longer independent because the missing phase overlapped those lines.

